To trigger the signing of all UKIs and the bootloader binary, we will run the
following commands:
pacman -S systemd
bootctl update

Re-installing systemd will trigger a pacman hook, which in turn will trigger
signing of the bootloader binaries. A default pacman hook will also trigger,
causing the UKIs to be rebuilt. During this process, systemd-ukify will take
care of signing the generated UKIs. "bootctl update" will copy the updated
(signed) bootloader EFI binaries to the EFI system partition.
